{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And HaShem has set you apart this day.</b> In that He enters into covenant with you and did not do so for any other nation, He has given you superiority in this respect." "<b>To be to Him a treasured people.</b> In order that He may achieve through you what He desires to achieve from the human species, as it says: נַעֲשֶׂה אָדָם בְּצַלְמֵנוּ כִּדְמוּתֵנוּ (Genesis 1:26)." "<b>And to keep all His commandments.</b> And He has given you superiority also in that He chose you to keep all His commandments, through which you find favor in His eyes. The rest of the nations, before Him, are not prepared and fit for this, as the Sages of blessed memory said: גּוֹי שֶׁשָּׁבַת חַיָּב מִיתָה (Sanhedrin 58b). Accordingly they are not fit to keep all His commandments, but only some of them — which are the commandments of the children of Noah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:19.080668329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}